+# Codex Desktop marker carrier amendment
+
+Live #96 qualification stopped on the exact protected trunk release `c2f3582d07d0f3dfeb680ab565fb3a5c5339d2ac` from PR #97. The actual registered Codex Desktop client recorded the canonical single-line marker wrapper followed by one transport line feed. Its native tool result joined to the exact queued command. A second distinct single-line call repeated the same transport suffix. The released U04 full-match parser rejected the first call before validating the receipt. No production installation, Claude workload or Core activity followed. Keep the original source and live evidence.
+
+## Owner and verification
+
+U04 / #88 owns a narrow carrier compatibility fix in the Codex adapter and its tests. The Desktop client exposed this carrier shape. Accept zero or one final ASCII line feed for every otherwise exact marker wrapper that reaches the existing supported Codex scanner and adapter route. The scanner still requires its already approved client and format. Interpret the final line feed only as carrier framing and leave the remaining canonical wrapper, typed command and opaque receipt validation unchanged. Reject other trailing or leading bytes, alternate whitespace, extra code, unsupported wrapper shapes, mismatched commands, output and receipt identity, and uncertain native tool order. No generic stripping, parsing of arbitrary code, or wider source admission. Preserve all existing accounting and privacy behavior. Add the exact retained shape as a sanitized positive regression and explicit negative shape coverage.
+
+Verify RED on the exact released code, GREEN with genuine same-session tool evidence and existing adapter tests, and a read-only or disposable-state proof against the original unmodified authorized #96 native record. Confirm the actual queued command's receipt and first request can be joined through the approved scanner/adapter path, with zero use admitted outside authorized scope. Run the full serial locked suite and retain exact independent source review. Deliver the small reviewed fix through a normal protected-trunk PR. Verify its exact merge tree and wheel before using it for qualification.
+
+## Sequencing and estimates
+
+Return #83 and #96 to Planning until this amendment passes SAR, independent SPR and native XPR on the exact bytes. Reopen #88 in its existing dedicated worktree on exact protected trunk `c2f3582d07d0f3dfeb680ab565fb3a5c5339d2ac`. Any remote base drift requires a fresh pin. Preserve prior U04 source acceptance and add a separate repair receipt. Only resume #96 on the exact independently accepted and delivered source with a fresh reviewed JIT. Early authorization, costs and original provider-native inputs may carry forward with their original provenance. Reprocess any reused exact provider inputs with the repaired wheel. No old-wheel ledger row, cursor, status, heartbeat, rehearsal outcome or receipt field qualifies the repaired release. The first diagnostic did not retain the required pre-poll capture time, so repeat that actual case. Recreate every mandatory collector-produced proof with the repaired merge tree and wheel. Repeat the actual isolated proof and required rehearsal before production installation, and validate the full real receipt before closing #83. Keep the same project identity and eventual ledger, and leave Core #2 outside execution.
+
+The four agent-hour U04 and U11 caps and 48.5-hour epic estimate remain in force. U11 includes the existing 0.5 agent-hour actual controlled workload cap. Stop before any ownership or forecast deviation. This amendment fixes a verified native carrier difference without changing the lifetime scope, metrics, installed command or later C44 handoff.
+
+## Cumulative forecast
+
+Allow up to 0.75 agent-hour for the U04 repair, focused review and locked verification on top of its earlier recorded work. The earlier observed implementation intervals were about 35 minutes, with prior review and coordinator verification tracked separately. Allow up to 2.5 agent-hours for the resumed U11 non-workload qualification, including the fresh protected artifact and isolated rehearsal, within the existing 3.5-hour non-workload portion. The first U11 attempt took about ten calendar minutes from pickup to diagnostic, including about 113 seconds from the first live marker to diagnosis. Retain these as observed intervals without inventing engagement time. Charge all earlier and repeated work cumulatively to each existing leaf allowance. The 0.5 agent-hour controlled workload allowance is also cumulative. These forecasts fit the remaining caps. Stop and replan before a forecast overrun.
